Fixed networks for brobdicube -D (copies of the files in ../algs3):
  W61   the worst-case planner's 61-stage network (n >= 2^24; at 2^19..2^23
        it uses the other 001111-0024 variant, 33e26fff...)
  A61a  the average planner's 61-stage network at n ~ 10^7 .. 10^8
  A61b  the average planner's 61-stage network at n >= ~10^8
With only these files brobdicube can still choose orientations, widths and
(unless -g / -O) greedy or optimal planning per phase.

  P72   permnet72 (the separate permnet72 solver): net241212 (32 stages, splits U L F from
        R B D) and net12444 (20 stages) for each half, 72 stages in all.
        Made from permnet72 -d, which prints each stage's move sequence in
        the order applied; a file lists stage 0 first, so each network's
        sequences are in reverse print order.  The name is
        key-stages-v-h-o-c-hash (v/h/o/c as brobdicube counts them, hash =
        FNV-1a of the lines, as pareto.cpp; only an identifier).
        Checks (2026-10-09): every solve of n = 4..11, -g and -O, -p 1 and
        64, replays as solved in tests/cubesim.py; with -g the per-stage
        usage probabilities equal permnet72's exactly.  With -O the mean
        number of stages equals permnet72 -m's (9.0041 outer, 6.3682 inner)
        but ties between equally short plans are broken differently, so the
        per-stage probabilities differ.  The two inner files have the same
        canonical key, so brobdicube uses the cheaper one (rotated) for both
        halves, where permnet72 uses its own sequences for each half.
